 "_doc": "THE IMPULSE BANK — a bigger batch of impulses, a wider pitch variety (his word 2026-10-06, DEC-37; RUNNING_LOG §193): the sounds the electronics draw on beyond the opening's six per player. One row per impulse: `n` continues the player's series (the opening's are 1 … 6, so the batch is 7 on — the name `<player>-impulse-<n>` is the sample's identity through the piece) · `inst` the lane's recipe key (sandbox/instruments.js) · `technique` the recipe's key on that lane · `key` the MIDI key · `label` what it is, in words. The percussionist has TWO instruments (the percussion lane and the mallets' lane, one microphone), so his batch is longer. tools/build_impulse_bank.js reads this and writes scores/impulse-bank.json: part one the notes with a mic opening over each (round robin across the players, `gapS` apart); part two, `returnsAfterS` later, THREE return bricks per sample (`variantsPerSample`), dealt presets by tools/deal_variants.js — the processed versions the three body problem's computer players draw on. HIS PASS with the engine up banks the batch and renders the variants as they are captured. HIS DATA — a key, a technique or a row changed here, then the tool again (--replace), then File ▾ → Reload. The flute's keys stay under 72: its presets' zones are unmeasured beyond the slap's (48 … 64, RUNNING_LOG §74) and a key outside a zone is silent or a function key.",
